VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the release chain is modern. The CLI publishes to NPM through OIDC trusted publishing, so there are no long-lived tokens anywhere in the pipeline, and every installer ships with SHA-256 sidecars. The first release candidate'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'only landed on June 20th. Everything you are about to see was built in public in a matter of months. Getting a server from zero to shipping takes four commands. NPM install OpenShift globally, or pipe their install script'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if that is more your style. OpenShift up registers it as a background service that starts on boot and restarts itself if it dies. Then, inside any project, OpenShift init links the directory, and OpenShift'

